1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:05,935
This is SignalHarbor, Dhruv Thacker’s submission for the S and P Global and Crisil Campus
Hackathon.

2
00:00:05,935 --> 00:00:12,583
It turns news and community text into an inspectable risk signal, then explores a
hypothetical portfolio impact.

3
00:00:12,583 --> 00:00:17,984
This edited walkthrough uses captures of the working application and synthesized
narration.

4
00:00:17,984 --> 00:00:20,774
The default replay contains fictional examples.

5
00:00:20,774 --> 00:00:26,887
Fourteen inputs become thirteen unique signals, three stress triggers, and six items
requiring review..

6
00:00:28,087 --> 00:00:34,371
The public repository includes all code, datasets, a seven slide presentation, and an M I
T license.

7
00:00:34,371 --> 00:00:41,031
With Node version twenty two or newer, run npm start and open localhost on port eighty
seven eighty seven.

8
00:00:41,031 --> 00:00:43,859
No package installation or API key is needed.

9
00:00:43,859 --> 00:00:48,446
The same original JavaScript engine runs in the browser and the Node API.

10
00:00:48,446 --> 00:00:52,027
JSON outputs preserve the evidence behind each decision..

11
00:00:53,227 --> 00:00:59,157
This fictional geopolitical report contains war, sanctions, invasion, and a shipping
blockade.

12
00:00:59,157 --> 00:01:04,204
The engine assigns negative sentiment, the geopolitical class, and severity ten.

13
00:01:04,204 --> 00:01:11,017
A multinomial Naive Bayes classifier learns unigram and bigram features from eighty four
synthetic examples.

14
00:01:11,017 --> 00:01:14,487
Sentiment uses a financial lexicon with local negation.

15
00:01:14,487 --> 00:01:16,632
Severity is an explicit heuristic.

16
00:01:16,632 --> 00:01:20,417
Contributing terms and machine readable output stay visible.

17
00:01:20,417 --> 00:01:24,770
Model scores are uncalibrated, not probabilities of market outcomes..

18
00:01:25,970 --> 00:01:32,987
The selected signal passes the automatic trigger: severity above seven, negative
sentiment, and no review flag.

19
00:01:32,987 --> 00:01:40,004
Module B applies transparent shocks to eleven synthetic positions across loans, bonds,
derivatives, and equity.

20
00:01:40,004 --> 00:01:46,453
At severity ten, the one hundred million dollar portfolio falls to ninety two point three
two million.

21
00:01:46,453 --> 00:01:52,395
The seven point six eight million loss combines rate, spread, equity, and loan credit
effects.

22
00:01:52,395 --> 00:01:55,367
These are scenario assumptions, not forecasts..

23
00:01:56,567 --> 00:02:03,430
Moving the severity slider from ten to five scales the shocks and halves the loss to three
point eight four million dollars.

24
00:02:03,430 --> 00:02:06,751
The rate shock becomes thirty seven point five basis points.

25
00:02:06,751 --> 00:02:09,408
Each scenario starts from the original baseline.

26
00:02:09,408 --> 00:02:13,836
Events do not compound the losses, and the interface marks the analyst override.

27
00:02:13,836 --> 00:02:17,434
The rate hedge is included with its correct signed contribution..

28
00:02:18,634 --> 00:02:23,574
Switching to the Aster credit event changes the scope to matching issuer positions.

29
00:02:23,574 --> 00:02:28,515
The stressed portfolio value is approximately ninety six point two million dollars.

30
00:02:28,515 --> 00:02:30,598
Unrelated issuers remain unchanged.

31
00:02:30,598 --> 00:02:35,717
A pay fixed rate swap can gain when rates rise, even while other exposures lose value.

32
00:02:35,717 --> 00:02:39,883
An unmatched issuer produces a warning and zero issuer specific loss..

33
00:02:41,083 --> 00:02:43,057
The monitor also accepts new text.

34
00:02:43,057 --> 00:02:50,371
Here the input is an unconfirmed rumor that Harbor Logistics could be hit by ransomware,
with the source set to a social post.

35
00:02:50,371 --> 00:02:54,377
This tests uncertainty handling alongside the core event extraction..

36
00:02:55,577 --> 00:02:59,413
The result is a cyber or operational event with negative sentiment.

37
00:02:59,413 --> 00:03:01,760
Qualified wording caps severity at seven.

38
00:03:01,760 --> 00:03:07,256
The report is flagged for human review because it is unconfirmed and comes from a social
source.

39
00:03:07,256 --> 00:03:09,947
It does not create an automatic stress trigger.

40
00:03:09,947 --> 00:03:13,840
Users can still explore a clearly identified hypothetical scenario..

41
00:03:15,040 --> 00:03:19,934
Live mode polls official Federal Reserve news and Hacker News community story titles.

42
00:03:19,934 --> 00:03:22,812
This run returned twelve records from each source.

43
00:03:22,812 --> 00:03:25,576
Publication times and source links are retained.

44
00:03:25,576 --> 00:03:29,721
All twenty four current records require review and none triggers stress.

45
00:03:29,721 --> 00:03:35,133
A network error is displayed explicitly; synthetic records never replace a failed live
source.

46
00:03:35,133 --> 00:03:41,120
The static hosted demo supports replay and analysis, while live polling requires the local
Node server..

47
00:03:42,320 --> 00:03:45,219
Twenty two functional and H T T P tests passed.

48
00:03:45,219 --> 00:03:56,011
The event model correctly classifies all twenty eight supplied diagnostic examples, but
both training and evaluation are small, synthetic, and from the same author and domain.

49
00:03:56,011 --> 00:03:58,662
This does not establish real news accuracy.

50
00:03:58,662 --> 00:04:05,754
Local engine p ninety five latency was zero point four zero seven milliseconds, excluding
networking and rendering.

51
00:04:05,754 --> 00:04:13,031
Next steps are independent finance data, calibrated uncertainty, better entity linking,
and full instrument repricing.

52
00:04:13,031 --> 00:04:15,806
AI assistance is disclosed in the repository.

53
00:04:15,806 --> 00:04:20,308
The code and presentation make every result reproducible and reviewable..
